<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Porcius Cato (consul 114 BCE)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Porcius Cato was a Roman politician, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cato-the-elder">Cato the Elder</a>, who was consul in 114 BCE. As governor of Macedonia he led an army against the Scordisci in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, where it was destroyed, a defeat that opened a long series of Roman wars on the Balkan frontier. He was later convicted of taking bribes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a> of Numidia and went into exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarraco">Tarraco</a>.</p></div>
